{
  "about": "A Cell Format holds Font, Fill and Borders beside the Number Format and the Alignment (ADR-0071, SH-38, SH-44), recorded at cell, row and column level, and set by a change that names only the parts it sets, its Borders relative to each range. Each cell records its own four sides, and the edge two cells share shows one line from either side, as the eleventh, twelfth and fourteenth Windows runs found Excel's to. Transcribed from CellFormatTests.cs.",
